---
layout: null
permalink: /feed-en.xml
---
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom">
  <title>{{ site.title }} - English Digest</title>
  <link href="{{ '/feed-en.xml' | absolute_url }}" rel="self"/>
  <link href="{{ '/' | absolute_url }}"/>
  <updated>{{ site.time | date_to_xmlschema }}</updated>
  <id>{{ '/' | absolute_url }}</id>
  {% assign takes = site.commentary | where_exp: "c", "c.title" | sort: "date" | reverse %}
  {% for take in takes limit:5 %}
  <entry>
    <title>Commentary: {{ take.title | escape }}</title>
    <link href="{{ take.url | absolute_url }}"/>
    <updated>{{ take.date | date_to_xmlschema }}</updated>
    <id>{{ take.url | absolute_url }}</id>
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[ {{ take.content }} ]]></content>
  </entry>
  {% endfor %}
  {%- comment -%}
  A run that publishes nothing still writes its page, which is right: the
  page carries the health footer and proves the run happened. The feed
  entry has no reader value, and after a quiet run it is the first thing a
  new subscriber sees. Excluded here rather than by not writing the page.

  "!= 0" rather than "> 0" on purpose: posts written before the item count
  was added to front matter have no `items` field at all, and a nil count
  means unknown rather than empty. Exclude only what is known to be zero.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% assign en_posts = site.posts | where: "lang", "en" | where_exp: "p", "p.items != 0" %}
  {% for post in en_posts limit:7 %}
  <entry>
    <title>{{ post.title | escape }}</title>
    <link href="{{ post.url | absolute_url }}"/>
    <updated>{{ post.date | date_to_xmlschema }}</updated>
    <id>{{ post.url | absolute_url }}</id>
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[ {{ post.content }} ]]></content>
  </entry>
  {% endfor %}
</feed>
